IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgd-acquisition`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- the compulsory acquisition of the shares of dissenting shareholders after a take-over offer (s 215), and joint offers (s 215AA), as ONE CHAIN of steps,
-- a regulative layer over the Boolean encoding in sgd-acquisition.l4. The gates are the existing section functions, called and not restated.
-- The chain, each clock measured from its own trigger: the offer is made; the holders of not less than 90% approve it within 4 months after the offer (s 215(1));
-- the transferee gives notice to a dissenting shareholder within 2 months after the approval (s 215(1)); the dissenting shareholder may apply to the Court within one month from the notice,
-- or within 14 days of a statement being supplied, whichever is the later (s 215(1)); then, the Court not having ordered to the contrary, the transferee transmits the notice with the instrument of transfer and pays (s 215(4)).
-- Beside the chain: the dissenter's demand for the other dissenters' names (s 215(2)); the election between alternative terms (s 215(1A), (1B));
-- the sell-out leg once transfers reach 90% (s 215(3)); the company's registration, bank account and trust (ss 215(4), (5)); the transfer to the Official Receiver and what the Official Receiver does (ss 215(6), (7)); the joint notice (s 215AA(6)).
-- Parties are the corpus's own `Party` (sg-core.l4). Every month or year period is turned into a number of days by sg-periods from DATE inputs, because a TRACE has no calendar:
-- each DATE input must agree with the day of the trace on which that event happens (day 0 of the trace is the first trigger named in the rule's TIMELINE line).
-- Where a step is a power with a time limit (MAY ... WITHIN), a missed limit is not a breach: the text states no consequence except that the power is gone, so LEST is FULFILLED.
-- Where a step is a duty with no last day in the text, it carries no WITHIN and no LEST (a LEST on a clock-less MUST can never be reached).

DECLARE `s 215 chain act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1) the holders of not less than 90% of the shares approve the scheme or contract`
    `s 215(1) the transferee gives notice to the dissenting shareholder that it desires to acquire the shares`
    `s 215(1) the dissenting shareholder applies to the Court for an order that the transferee is not bound to acquire the shares`
    `s 215(1) the Court orders that the transferee is not entitled and bound to acquire the shares`
    `s 215(1) the Court disposes of the application without ordering to the contrary`
    `s 215(1A) the dissenting shareholder elects which of the alternative terms the shareholder prefers`
    `s 215(1B) the transferee states in the offer which of the alternative terms is to apply on a failure to elect`
    `s 215(2) the dissenting shareholder serves a written demand for the statement of the names and addresses of the other dissenting shareholders`
    `s 215(2) the transferor company supplies the statement and posts it to the dissenting shareholder`
    `s 215(3)(a) the transferee gives notice that the transfers have reached 90% to the holders of the remaining shares who have not assented`
    `s 215(3)(b) the holder requires the transferee to acquire the shares in question`
    `s 215(3) the transferee acquires the shares that the holder requires it to acquire`
    `s 215(4)(a) the transferee transmits a copy of the notice and the executed instrument of transfer to the transferor company`
    `s 215(4)(b) the transferee pays, allots or transfers the price of the shares to the transferor company`
    `s 215(4) the transferor company registers the transferee as the holder of the shares`
    `s 215(5) the transferor company pays the sums it received into a separate bank account`
    `s 215(5) the transferor company holds the sums and other consideration in trust for the persons entitled`
    `s 215(6) the company holding the money or other consideration transfers it to the Official Receiver`
    `s 215(7)(a) the Official Receiver deals with the moneys as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 215(7)(b) the Official Receiver sells or disposes of the other consideration and deals with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197`
    `s 215AA(6) a joint transferee joins in making the notice, and a joint transferee that is a company has a director sign it`

§ `Helpers: periods turned into days`

-- A month or a year has no fixed number of days, so the length of each window is the number of days from the day of its trigger to the last day of the period (sg-periods P1, P4).
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
      `the number of units` IS A NUMBER
      `the unit` IS A `Period unit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215 chain: the days from the event to the last day of a period after it` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the event` `the number of units` `the unit`) MINUS `the day of the event`

-- "within one month from the date on which the notice was given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied (whichever is the later)": the days from the notice to the last day of the later.
GIVEN `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(1) chain: the days from the notice to the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` MEANS
    (`s 215(1) the last day of the later of the one month and the 14 days` `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)` `the day the statement was supplied under subsection (2), if one was`) MINUS `the day the notice was given under subsection (1)`

§ `Section 215(4): the transferee's duties once the notice has been given`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the first day on which the transferee must act, which is the day after the end of the later of the one month after the notice and the 14 days after the statement, or the day after the Court disposes of a pending application (the existing function `s 215(4) the first day on which the transferee must act` gives the date); counting="after the expiration of one month after the date on which the notice has been given or, after 14 days after a statement has been supplied ... or if an application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending, after that application has been disposed of" (the text sets the earliest day and no last day, so no clock is encoded and nothing here can be breached by delay)
-- FORK: s 215(4) | (a) the copy of the notice with the instrument of transfer, and (b) the payment, are joined by "and" and not put in an order, so each is a MUST open from day 0, in either order (RAND) | (a) before (b)
-- FORK: s 215(4) | the earliest day is not a prohibition: a transmission or payment made before the one month or the 14 days is not a breach, because the text says the transferee "must, after" and states no bar before it; the chain below reaches this rule only after the dissenter's window has ended or the Court has disposed of the application | an early payment as a breach
-- FORK: s 215(4) | "or if an application ... is then pending, after that application has been disposed of" is read as the later of the end of the window and the disposal, as the existing function does (F-215-14 in sgd-acquisition.l4) | the disposal alone, even where it comes before the end of the window
-- src:20741 | (4) Where a notice has been given by the transferee under
-- src:20742 | subsection (1) and the Court has not, on an application made by
-- src:20743 | the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary, the transferee
-- src:20744 | must, after the expiration of one month after the date on which the
-- src:20745 | notice has been given or, after 14 days after a statement has been
-- src:20746 | supplied to a dissenting shareholder pursuant to subsection (2) or if an
-- src:20747 | application to the Court by the dissenting shareholder is then pending,
-- src:20748 | after that application has been disposed of —
-- src:20750 | (a) transmit a copy of the notice to the transferor company
-- src:20751 | together with an instrument of transfer executed, on behalf
-- src:20752 | of the shareholder by any person appointed by the
-- src:20753 | transferee, and on its own behalf by the transferee; and
-- src:20755 | (b) pay, allot or transfer to the transferor company the amount
-- src:20756 | or other consideration representing the price payable by the
-- src:20757 | transferee for the shares which by virtue of this section the
-- src:20758 | transferee is entitled to acquire,
-- src:20760 | and the transferor company must thereupon register the transferee as
