@ref s 215(4) the transferee's duties after the notice (src:20741-20761)
GIVEN transferee IS A Party
      `a notice has been given by the transferee under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has, on an application made by the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 chain act`
`s 215(4) chain: the transferee must transmit the notice and pay, but only once a notice has been given and the Court has not ordered to the contrary` MEANS
    IF (`s 215(4) the transferee must transmit a copy of the notice and pay, allot or transfer the consideration to the transferor company` `a notice has been given by the transferee under subsection (1)` `the Court has, on an application made by the dissenting shareholder, ordered to the contrary`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN ((PARTY transferee
           MUST `s 215(4)(a) the transferee transmits a copy of the notice and the executed instrument of transfer to the transferor company`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
          RAND
          (PARTY transferee
           MUST `s 215(4)(b) the transferee pays, allots or transfers the price of the shares to the transferor company`
           HENCE FULFILLED))
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 215(1): the approval, the notice, the application to the Court and the payment, as one chain`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the transferee makes the offer; counting="within 4 months after the making of the offer" for the approval (the window opens the day after the offer, sg-periods P2; the last day is the offer day plus 4 months, from the DATE input of the offer day); each later step is chained by HENCE, so its clock restarts on the day the step before it is done: "within 2 months, after the offer has been so approved" runs from the approval day (a DATE input that must equal the trace day on which the approval happens); "within one month from the date on which the notice was given or within 14 days of a statement being supplied ... (whichever is the later)" runs from the notice day and the statement day (two DATE inputs that must equal the trace days); the payment duty is the rule above, reached only through the notice
-- FORK: s 215(1) | the approval by the holders is a MAY of the holders with a limit of 4 months, and a lapse ends the chain with nothing owed (FULFILLED) | the approval as something that happens outside the rule, supplied as a Boolean
-- FORK: s 215(1) | a notice outside the 2 months, or a notice to a shareholder who is not dissenting, or a notice not in the prescribed manner, is no notice under subsection (1): the existing gate does not answer JUST TRUE and the chain ends with nothing owed | a late or irregular notice as a breach by the transferee
-- FORK: s 215(1) | "supplied" is read as the day the statement is posted (subsection (2)), as the existing function does (F-215-5 in sgd-acquisition.l4) | the day the statement is received
-- FORK: s 215(1) | the Court's order is a MAY of the Court with no time limit (the text has none): to order otherwise ends the chain, and to dispose of the application without ordering otherwise sends the transferee to its duties in subsection (4) | the Court's silence as a refusal
-- Where no application is made in time the transferee's duties of subsection (4) follow at once (LEST of the application step): the text makes the transferee "entitled and bound" "when such a notice is given" unless the Court orders otherwise.
