§ `Section 215(2): the dissenting shareholder's demand for the other dissenting shareholders' names`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the transferee gave notice to the dissenting shareholder under subsection (1); counting="within one month from the date on which the notice was given" for the demand (the last day is the notice day plus one month, from the DATE input of the notice day); the company's duty to supply the statement has no day in the text (silent), and the 14 days after the posting, until which the transferee is not entitled or bound to acquire, are carried by the application window of the chain above
-- FORK: s 215(2) | the demand is a MAY of the dissenting shareholder and the statement a MUST of the transferor company with no limit; a missed month ends the demand and nothing is owed (FULFILLED) | the company's statement as a duty with a deadline the text does not give
-- The existing function `s 215(2) the dissenting shareholder is entitled to require the transferor company to supply the statement` folds the one month and the demand day into one answer, which the clock here carries, so the gate is the Boolean that the notice has been given.
