    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 215(4) and (5): the transferor company registers, banks and holds in trust`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the transferor company receives the copy of the notice, the instrument of transfer and the price from the transferee; counting="thereupon" for the registration and silent for subsection (5) (no day is named, so no clock is encoded and none of the three duties has a breach path of its own)
-- FORK: s 215(4), (5) | registration and the two duties of subsection (5) are three MUSTs of the transferor company open together from the day it receives (RAND) | registration first, then the bank account, then the trust
-- FORK: s 215(5) | the duty to pay into a separate bank account is owed only for "sums" (money); where only other consideration was received, only registration and the trust are owed | the bank account for any consideration
-- src:20760 | and the transferor company must thereupon register the transferee as
-- src:20761 | the holder of those shares.
-- src:20765 | (5) Any sums received by the transferor company under this section
-- src:20766 | must be paid into a separate bank account, and any such sums and any
-- src:20767 | other consideration so received must be held by the transferor
-- src:20768 | company in trust for the several persons entitled to the shares in
-- src:20769 | respect of which they were respectively received.
@ref s 215(4), (5) registration, bank account and trust (src:20760-20769)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      `the transferor company has received the copy of the notice, the instrument of transfer and the price from the transferee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor company received sums of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 chain act`
`s 215(4) and (5) chain: the transferor company must register the transferee, bank the sums and hold them in trust once it has received them` MEANS
    IF `the transferor company has received the copy of the notice, the instrument of transfer and the price from the transferee`
    THEN ((PARTY company
           MUST `s 215(4) the transferor company registers the transferee as the holder of the shares`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
          RAND
          (PARTY company
           MUST `s 215(5) the transferor company holds the sums and other consideration in trust for the persons entitled`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
          RAND
          (IF `the transferor company received sums of money`
           THEN (PARTY company
                 MUST `s 215(5) the transferor company pays the sums it received into a separate bank account`
                 HENCE FULFILLED)
           ELSE FULFILLED))
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 215(6) and (7): the transfer to the Official Receiver`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it; counting="after the expiration of 2 years and must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which the money or other consideration was received": the 2 years end on the day received plus 2 years and the 10 years on the day received plus 10 years (sg-periods P1, P4, from the DATE input of the day received), the second window being chained by HENCE from the end of the first (so its length is the 10 years less the 2 years); the Official Receiver's duties have no day (silent)
-- FORK: s 215(6) | a transfer on or before the last day of the 2 years is outside the permission and is a BREACH by the company, although the text states no consequence | a transfer that is early merely not authorised, with no breach
-- FORK: s 215(6) | "before the expiration of 10 years" is read as up to and including the last day of the 10 years (the existing function does the same, and so does section 210(10A)) | the day before the last day
-- FORK: s 215(6) | "received by the person" is read as received by the company holding it, as the existing function does (finding 3 in NOTES.md) | the day the person became entitled
-- FORK: s 215(7) | the Official Receiver's two duties are alternatives chosen by what was received (money, or other consideration), each a MUST with no limit and no breach path | both owed on every transfer
-- src:20773 | (6) Where any money or other consideration is held in trust by a
-- src:20774 | company for any person under this section, the company holding the
-- src:20775 | money or other consideration may, after the expiration of 2 years and
-- src:20776 | must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which the
-- src:20778 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026
-- src:20779 | 2020 Ed. Companies Act 1967 420
-- src:20781 | money or other consideration was received by the person, transfer the
-- src:20782 | money or other consideration to the Official Receiver.
-- src:20786 | (7) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:20788 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (6) as if
-- src:20789 | the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:20790 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20791 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:20793 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:20794 | subsection (6) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:20795 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:20796 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:20797 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20798 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 215(6), (7) the transfer to the Official Receiver and what the Official Receiver does (src:20773-20798)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      `money or other consideration is held in trust by a company for a person under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` IS A DATE
      `the thing received under subsection (6) is money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing received under subsection (6) is other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 chain act`
`s 215(6) and (7) chain: the company may transfer after 2 years and must before 10 years, then the Official Receiver deals with it` MEANS
    IF `money or other consideration is held in trust by a company for a person under this section`
    THEN PARTY company
         SHANT `s 215(6) the company holding the money or other consideration transfers it to the Official Receiver`
         WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the event to the last day of a period after it` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` 2 Years)
         HENCE (PARTY company
                MUST `s 215(6) the company holding the money or other consideration transfers it to the Official Receiver`
                WITHIN ((`s 215 chain: the days from the event to the last day of a period after it` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` 10 Years) MINUS (`s 215 chain: the days from the event to the last day of a period after it` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the company holding it` 2 Years))
                HENCE (IF `the thing received under subsection (6) is money`
                       THEN (PARTY `Official Receiver`
                             MUST `s 215(7)(a) the Official Receiver deals with the moneys as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
                             HENCE FULFILLED)
                       ELSE (IF `the thing received under subsection (6) is other consideration`
                             THEN (PARTY `Official Receiver`
                                   MUST `s 215(7)(b) the Official Receiver sells or disposes of the other consideration and deals with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197`
                                   HENCE FULFILLED)
                             ELSE FULFILLED))
                LEST BREACH BY company BECAUSE "the money or other consideration was not transferred to the Official Receiver before the expiration of 10 years from the date it was received")
         LEST BREACH BY company BECAUSE "the money or other consideration was transferred to the Official Receiver before the expiration of 2 years from the date it was received"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 215AA(6): the joint transferees' notice`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the joint transferees give a notice under section 215(1) or (3); counting=silent (the text gives subsection (6) no day of its own; the days of the notices are those of the rules above)
-- FORK: s 215AA(6) | the rule is written for two joint transferees, each a MUST joined by RAND, and the duty is gated by the existing test of section 215AA(1) (an offer for all the shares by 2 or more persons jointly); a third needs a third branch | one MUST of "all of the joint transferees" as a single party
-- s 215AA(4) (joint rights and joint and several obligations) and (5) (a notice to any one of them is a notice to all, subject to (6)) are not steps with a day and are not encoded here.
-- src:20949 | 215AA.—(1) In the case of a scheme involving an offer to acquire
-- src:20950 | all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in any particular
-- src:20951 | class in a company, by 2 or more persons jointly (called in this section
-- src:20952 | the joint transferees), section 215 is to be read subject to this section.
-- src:21001 | (6) The notice required to be given by the joint transferees under
-- src:21002 | section 215(1) and (3) must be made by all of the joint transferees
-- src:21003 | and, where one or more of them is a company, signed by a director of
-- src:21004 | that company.
@ref s 215AA(1), (6) the joint notice (src:20949-21004)
GIVEN `joint transferee one` IS A Party
      `joint transferee two` IS A Party
      `the scheme involves an offer to acquire all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in a particular class in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons making the offer jointly` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215 chain act`
`s 215AA(6) chain: the joint transferees must make the notice together` MEANS
    IF (`s 215AA(1) section 215 is to be read subject to section 215AA` `the scheme involves an offer to acquire all of the shares in a company, or all of the shares in a particular class in a company` `the number of persons making the offer jointly`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN ((PARTY `joint transferee one`
           MUST `s 215AA(6) a joint transferee joins in making the notice, and a joint transferee that is a company has a director sign it`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
          RAND
          (PARTY `joint transferee two`
           MUST `s 215AA(6) a joint transferee joins in making the notice, and a joint transferee that is a company has a director sign it`
           HENCE FULFILLED))
    ELSE FULFILLED
